WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:03.460
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday. Three things:
First, I went to Los Angeles a couple days

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:06.379
ago to watch a movie. I don't think I'm allowed to tell you the name of the movie, but I can hint

00:00:06.379 --> 00:00:11.139
at it. It comes out on June 6th, it's funny
but then other times it's very very sad,

00:00:11.139 --> 00:00:14.400
and I really, really loved it.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.640
So that's exciting and also a huge
relief. I need to change shirts because I match the wall.

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:21.530
All right, that's better. In a totally unrelated
story, everyone should read my book

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:25.199
The Fault in Our Stars before the movie
adaptation comes out on June 6th. Was I

00:00:25.199 --> 00:00:28.300
subtle? They said I needed to be subtle.
Secondly, AFC Wimbledon had their first

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.590
game as a team sponsored by Nerdfighteria.

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:34.200
Rosianna: I'm an internet kid and I love GIFs and
I love Instagram pictures

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.480
and I love YouTube videos, but there's something really quite cool to the physicality of it.

00:00:38.489 --> 00:00:42.920
To see those physical boards around a physical
pitch designed by physical Nerdfighters,

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:46.690
some of whom live half a physical world away
from me and from the stadium.

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:50.700
Wimbledon lost the game, but the long arc of
history bends towards justice, so we'll be fine.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.730
And lastly, I get to give away some
money. So Nerdfighters raised more than

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:57.989
860,000 dollars in this year's Project
for Awesome. After we pay to make and ship

00:00:57.989 --> 00:01:02.009
Project for Awesome perks, all the remaining
money goes to charities chosen by Nerdfighteria;

00:01:02.009 --> 00:01:07.340
and today I get to announce ten
winning charities that each receive 50,000 dollars.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:10.530
First the Harry Potter Alliance, which fights
inequality and illiteracy and once

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:13.450
worked with Nerdfighteria to send five
airplanes worth of life-saving medical

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:15.210
supplies to Haiti after the earthquake there.

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:18.670
Secondly, This Star Won't Go Out, the
organization set up in memory of Esther

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:22.090
Earl that provides direct support to
families of kids with cancer.

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:26.340
Then there's Not Forgotten; they house, feed,
and educate children in Peru. And fourth

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:30.360
we have Save the Children, which works
around the world to fight poverty and disease.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.520
Fifth, Liberty in North Korea,
which is one of those organizations that

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:36.160
helpfully puts its mission statement in its name.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:38.900
Sixth, Child's Play, which
provides gaming systems to kids in

00:01:38.909 --> 00:01:42.649
children's hospital so that they can beat
me at FIFA. Seventh and eighth, we have two water

00:01:42.649 --> 00:01:46.720
charities: The Thirst Project and Water.org
Ninth, we have Partners for

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:49.580
Mental Health, another one of those
organizations that tells you what it does in its name.

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:53.259
And lastly TECHO, which I'm probably
mispronouncing, an organization that

00:01:53.259 --> 00:01:56.759
mobilizes young people, including a group
of Nerdfighters in Argentina,

00:01:56.759 --> 00:02:00.570
to build houses for people living in
poverty around Latin America.

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:03.680
So Hank, all ten of those organizations will
receive 50,000 dollars a piece

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:06.829
from the Foundation to Decrease Worldsuck.
Now people are probably wondering "what

00:02:06.829 --> 00:02:09.690
are they gonna do with the remaining
360,000 dollars, are

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:13.250
they gonna spend it all on pizza and
corn dogs?" Sadly, no.

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:15.950
Some of that's going to go to producing and
shipping, like, the t-shirts and the Women of YouTube

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:20.280
calendar. However, most of it
will be split among ten more winning charities.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:23.080
They are: To Write Love on Her Arms, The
Office of Letters and Light, The World Food

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:28.120
Project, Feeding America, The Wayne Foundation, Pencils for Kids, Women for Women International,

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:32.900
First Book, Kiva.org, and Doctors Without Borders.
So there you have it, the twenty winning

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:35.769
charities from the 2013 Project for Awesome.

00:02:35.769 --> 00:02:39.360
Our money's going to go to fight disease
and poverty and illiteracy and injustice,

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:42.890
and I'm so grateful to everyone who
donated and also everyone who took the

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:45.980
time to vote so that we could be good
stewards of this money.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:48.420
If you want to learn more about these 
organizations, there are links in the doobly-doo.

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:52.580
Thank you again for being part of the Project for Awesome with us. As we say in my hometown,

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:55.010
DFTBA. Hank, I'll see you on Friday.

